{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 16,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Job answered and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have heard many such things:Miserable comforters are ye all.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall vain words have an end?\nOr what provoketh thee that thou answerest?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I also could speak as ye do;\nIf your soul were in my soul’s stead,\nI could join words together against you,\nAnd shake my head at you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I would strengthen you with my mouth,\nAnd the solace of my lips would assuage ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "your grief",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though I speak, my grief is not assuaged;\nAnd though I forbear, what am I eased?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But now he hath made me weary:\nThou hast made desolate all my company.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou hast laid fast hold on me, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " is a witness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "against me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ":\nAnd my leanness riseth up against me,\nIt testifieth to my face.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He hath torn me in his wrath, and persecuted me;\nHe hath gnashed upon me with his teeth:\nMine adversary sharpeneth his eyes upon me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have gaped upon me with their mouth;\nThey have smitten me upon the cheek reproachfully:\nThey gather themselves together against me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "God delivereth me to the ungodly,\nAnd casteth me into the hands of the wicked.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I was at ease, and he brake me asunder;\nYea, he hath taken me by the neck, and dashed me to pieces:\nHe hath also set me up for his mark.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His archers compass me round about;\nHe cleaveth my reins asunder, and doth not spare;\nHe poureth out my gall upon the ground.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He breaketh me with breach upon breach;\nHe runneth upon me like a giant.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have sewed sackcloth upon my skin,\nAnd have laid my horn in the dust.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My face is red with weeping,\nAnd on my eyelids is the shadow of death;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Although there is no violence in my hands,\nAnd my prayer is pure.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O earth, cover not thou my blood,\nAnd let my cry have no ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "resting",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "-place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even now, behold, my witness is in heaven,\nAnd he that voucheth for me is on high.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My friends scoff at me:",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "But",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mine eye poureth out tears unto God,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That he would maintain the right of a man with God,\nAnd of a son of man with his neighbor!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.16.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For when a few years are come,\nI shall go the way whence I shall not return.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
